WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.422
Boolean values represent True and False.

00:00:03.422 --> 00:00:08.262
They become especially important when we start writing conditions and filters.

00:00:08.262 --> 00:00:14.757
Zero converts to False. A nonzero number such as one becomes True.

00:00:14.757 --> 00:00:20.955
An empty string becomes False, while nonempty text such as “Hello” becomes True.

00:00:21.516 --> 00:00:25.303
This gives us a preview of the logic used in the next module.

00:00:25.303 --> 00:00:34.558
Programs often ask questions such as: does a value exist, is an amount above a threshold, or does a record meet a rule?

00:00:34.558 --> 00:00:38.350
Those questions eventually evaluate to True or False.
